                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea4e876b-fee5-354f-b17b-2f4d6cadf1bf",
                                        "entry_id": "ffdc9612-d019-304d-a6c1-a52c06742783",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Either of two not closely related flowering plants"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08d9cbeb-7df8-4f77-80bb-e3dcdcce6ac3",
                                                "sense_id": "ea4e876b-fee5-354f-b17b-2f4d6cadf1bf",
                                                "text": "So men haue learned many precious remedies for many diseases euen by brute [beasts], as we see by the swallow, who hath taught vs that the ioice of Celandine is singuler for the eies, for that she restoreth sight to her yong ones with Celandine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a475f4b8-82b7-4b73-8f6a-c64714231322",
                                                "sense_id": "ea4e876b-fee5-354f-b17b-2f4d6cadf1bf",
                                                "text": "If your mouth waters now, what had it done, / Cou’d you have seen our delicate fine thrushes / Hot from the spit, with myrtle-berries cramm’d, / And larded well with celandine and parsley, / Bob at your hungry lips, crying—Come eat me!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b6968d9-1199-4f7e-a254-7e64b95c73a0",
                                                "sense_id": "ea4e876b-fee5-354f-b17b-2f4d6cadf1bf",
                                                "text": "Buttercups, that will be seen,\nWhether we will see or no;\nOthers, too, of lofty mien;\nThey have done as worldlings do,\nTaken praise that should be thine,\nLittle, humble Celandine!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b0eee78-4eff-48bf-a329-cc1981eb32ef",
                                                "sense_id": "ea4e876b-fee5-354f-b17b-2f4d6cadf1bf",
                                                "text": "Coming suddenly round a corner into a glade of silver birch trees Edmund saw the ground covered in all directions with little yellow flowers—celandines."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be45dc68-1faa-43b7-b4da-34946c99fd41",
                                                "sense_id": "ea4e876b-fee5-354f-b17b-2f4d6cadf1bf",
                                                "text": "The poor but lovely bird sat there, posing among the celandines and wood anemones, wondering why its wing-tips were frozen together."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c57a452-efd7-3171-a024-e8166ec65269",
                                        "entry_id": "ffdc9612-d019-304d-a6c1-a52c06742783",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Either of two not closely related flowering plants:",
                                            "Greater celandine (Chelidonium majus)."
                                        ],
